{
  "_note": [
    "Carrier flight decks, for the ground charts.",
    "",
    "BMS gives a ship no outline, no model and no feature list — only deck points, and those run far past the bow",
    "because the same list carries the approach path (Hermes' span 1,867 ft against a real ship of 744). So the deck",
    "is not traced from them. It is BUILT from the published dimensions of the real ship, and only the ramp",
    "NUMBERING comes from BMS: each of its spots is matched to the nearest place a real deck parks an aircraft.",
    "",
    "Every figure is feet, measured from the ship's own axis (its centre line) and from amidships:",
    "  deckFt      the flight deck, bow to stern",
    "  stbdFt      deck edge to starboard of the axis",
    "  portFwdFt   deck edge to port forward of the angled deck — the narrow part of the deck",
    "  sponsonFt   deck edge to port at its widest: the angled-deck sponson on a CATOBAR ship, the deck-edge",
    "              sponson on the others. stbdFt + sponsonFt is the published maximum width.",
    "  kind        catobar (angled landing deck and catapults), ski (a ramp at the bow), flat (an amphibious deck)",
    "  angleDeg    how far the landing deck is angled off the axis, to port",
    "  stripLenFt / stripWidFt   the landing area",
    "  skiDeg      the ski jump at the bow, where there is one",
    "  islands     each { along, across, long, wide }: along is aft(-) / forward(+) of amidships, across is to",
    "              starboard(+) of the axis, both to the middle of the island",
    "  match       matched against the field's name, upper-cased, first hit wins, so put the specific first.",
    "",
    "Published dimensions per class; see docs/DATA-SOURCES.md for where each came from."
  ],
